{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -lc 'rtk read ~/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/references/spec.md ~/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/assets/spec.md ~/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/references/tasks.md ~/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/assets/tasks.md ~/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/references/index.md'", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -lc 'rtk read ~/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/references/spec.md ~/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/assets/spec.md ~/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/references/tasks.md ~/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/assets/tasks.md ~/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/references/index.md'", "aggregated_output": "Purpose: section rules for `specs/<id>/spec.md`. Template: `assets/spec.md`.\n\nFrontmatter: `id` as YYYY-MM-DD-slug; `kind`, feature or fix; `status`, draft, building or shipped; `summary`, one user-facing line reused in release notes; `request`, the sentence, issue or commits it started from; `issue`, optional, delete the line when there is none. The owner's go is `approved: {by: <owner>, via: <in session, a message link, or a PR>}`, added only when the user reports it, never inferred; git dates it. After a change to Why or What changes, remove the line; the owner's new go writes it back. The go is never a status.\n\nWhy: required. The problem, who has it, and what it costs to leave it, in 2 to 5 lines. No solution.\n\nWhat changes: required. Claims under `### Add · <domain>/<capability>`, `### Change · ...` and `### Remove · ...`, only the headings that apply, one per capability. A Change claim carries a `was:` line with the current text on main. A Remove claim carries a `reason:` line. A fix that changes no behavior writes \"No behavior change.\" and nothing else here. Claims read exactly as they will in behavior/.\n\nNot doing: required for a feature, optional for a fix. What is deliberately out, so scope can't creep silently. Not future ideas with no decision behind them.\n\nOpen questions: while drafting, only questions the owner can answer. Delete the section when empty; the owner can't say go before that. Questions the agent can answer from the code never go here.\n\nA spec past about 80 lines is two specs.\n---\nid: \"{{YYYY-MM-DD-slug}}\"\nkind: \"{{feature | fix}}\"\nstatus: draft\nsummary: \"{{one user-facing line; reused in release notes}}\"\nrequest: \"{{the sentence, issue or commits it started from}}\"\nissue: \"{{tracker key}}\"\n---\n# {{Title as a verb phrase}}\n\n## Why\n<!-- required: the problem, who has it, and what it costs to leave it, in 2 to 5 lines. No solution. -->\n\n## What changes\n<!-- required. A fix that changes no behavior writes \"No behavior change.\" and nothing else here.\nUse only the headings below that apply, one per capability.\nClaims read exactly as they will in behavior/, so spec-ship copies them without rewording. -->\n\n### Add · {{domain}}/{{capability}}\n- {{Actor}} {{does or sees something observable, present tense}} {#{{claim-id}}}\n  e.g. {{a concrete situation}} -> {{the observable result}}\n\n### Change · {{domain}}/{{capability}}\n- {{The claim as it should read}} {#{{existing-claim-id}}}\n  was: {{the current text on main}}\n  e.g. {{a concrete situation}} -> {{the observable result}}\n\n### Remove · {{domain}}/{{capability}}\n- {{The claim being removed}} {#{{existing-claim-id}}}\n  reason: {{why it stops being true}}\n\n## Not doing\n<!-- required for a feature, optional for a fix: what is deliberately out, so scope can't creep silently. -->\n\n## Open questions\n<!-- while drafting: questions only the owner can answer. Delete the section when empty;\nthe owner can't say go before that. -->\nPurpose: rules for `specs/<id>/tasks.md`. Template: `assets/tasks.md`.\n\nFrontmatter: `spec`, the spec id.\n\nAbove the tasks, one line per session, newest last, facts only and never a verdict: `Session YYYY-MM-DD: resumed at Tn; first message: \"<gist of the user's first message>\".` After a change mid-way, one more line: `Rechecked YYYY-MM-DD after: <the change>. T2 redo, T4 new, T5 dropped.`\n\nTasks: `- [ ] T<n> <imperative task> -> <claim IDs, or \"check: <command or observable result>\">`. Each task fits in one session. Numbers are never reused. A claim is written as `capability#id` when its bare ID is not unique in the spec. A task is ticked only when the claims it names are proven.\n\nUnder a task, at most two lines: `- note: <blocked, tried, why>` or `- redo: <what changed>`, the task unticked again. A dropped task is removed and named in the recheck line. Anything lasting in a note moves to plan.md or a decision record.\n\nNothing else: no design discussion, no why.\n---\nspec: \"{{spec id}}\"\n---\n<!-- One line per session, above the tasks, newest last. Facts only, never a verdict:\nSession {{YYYY-MM-DD}}: resumed at {{Tn}}; first message: \"{{gist of the user's first message}}\".\nAfter a change mid-way, add one more line:\nRechecked {{YYYY-MM-DD}} after: {{the change}}. {{T2 redo, T4 new, T5 dropped}}. -->\n\n- [ ] T1 {{imperative task}} -> {{claim IDs, or \"check: <command or observable result>\"}}\n\n<!-- Rules:\n- Each task fits in one session. Numbers are never reused.\n- A claim is written as capability#id when its bare ID is not unique in the spec.\n- Under a task, at most two lines:\n    - note: blocked, tried, why\n    - redo: what changed (the task is unticked again)\n- A dropped task is removed and named in the recheck line.\n- Anything lasting in a note moves into plan.md or a decision record. -->\nPurpose: rules for `index.md`. Template: `assets/index.md`.\n\nFrontmatter: `product`, the product name; `docs-format`, the template version the project uses; `issue-tracker`, optional, the address a ticket key is appended to, such as `https://example.atlassian.net/browse/`, deleted when the team has none.\n\nWhat it is: who uses the product and for what, in 2 to 4 sentences, in the user's words. Not a feature list.\n\nDomains: a table with at least one row: domain, what it covers, owner. docs-init asks for the first row. spec-start and docs-map add a row the moment a new domain is named, before any go is asked. The owner is who says go for that domain; on a solo project, that is the user. A domain's behavior lives at `behavior/<domain>/`, so there is no link column.\n\nBehavior: one line pointing at `behavior/`, so an agent that loads only what index.md links to finds the claims. Architecture: one line pointing at `architecture/`.\n\nNothing else: details of any domain belong in behavior/.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
