{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_21", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/zsh -lc 'rtk read docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/spec.md docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/tasks.md'", "aggregated_output": "---\nid: 2026-10-13-customer-wishlist\nkind: feature\nstatus: draft\nsummary: Customers can save items to a wishlist.\nrequest: Customers can save items to a wishlist.\n---\n# Save items to a wishlist\n\n## Why\n\nThe customer problem is awaiting Sanne's answer to round 1, question 1.\nThe cost of leaving it unresolved has not yet been established.\n\n## What changes\n\n### Add · wishlist/save-items\n\n- Customers can save an item to a wishlist. {#save-item}\n  e.g. A customer saves a headlamp -> the headlamp is included in their wishlist.\n\n## Not doing\n\nScope exclusions await Sanne's answer to round 1, question 4.\n\n## Open questions\n\n1. What customer problem should this solve first, and what does that problem cost customers today?\n   This determines the outcome the feature must deliver.\n   Recommended: Help customers remember gear for a later purchase without searching for it again.\n\n2. Should guests be able to save items, or only signed-in customers?\n   This determines who can use the feature and whether saving requires an account.\n   Recommended: Start with signed-in customers.\n\n3. Should the new wishlist domain cover saving, viewing and removing saved items?\n   This sets its boundary; Sanne is already recorded as its owner.\n   Recommended: Yes, keep those three actions together in wishlist.\n\n4. Is one private list per customer enough for the first release?\n   This determines the initial scope and what is deliberately excluded.\n   Recommended: Yes; exclude sharing, multiple named lists and price or stock alerts.\n\n5. Map wishlist first?\n   There is no behavior/wishlist/ documentation; a mapping pass would check for existing behavior before the spec is settled.\n   Recommended: Skip a separate mapping pass for now and define the new behavior in this spec.\n---\nspec: 2026-10-13-customer-wishlist\n---\n\nSession 2026-10-13: resumed at T1; first message: \"Start a wishlist spec; Sanne owns every domain and is in the session; ask the first grilling round and stop.\"\n\n- [ ] T1 Settle the feature's why, domain boundary and scope with Sanne -> check: Sanne's answers are recorded in spec.md and all owner questions are resolved\n  - note: First round prepared; the user requested a stop after asking it.\n- [ ] T2 Create the customer-wishlist branch from main while retaining the existing project documentation -> check: the active branch is customer-wishlist and the existing project documentation is retained\n  - note: git switch -c customer-wishlist main failed because the sandbox cannot create the worktree's Git index.lock; the active branch remains dogfood-codex.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
